  "releaseNotes": "- Codex and OpenCode can resume an interrupted task in its original conversation. After a native process restart, the bridge checks identifiable workspace files and continues from recorded results. Operations with uncertain external effects are left for review.\n- The model Gateway retries a temporary task authorization renewal failure and can use a still-valid signed lease. Reports renewal outages separately from rejected task authorization and upstream API key errors.\n- Ships Runtime 1.0.1 with the matching native bridges and model Gateway.\n- Restarts a missing sandbox model Gateway during active Codex and OpenCode tasks. Tasks sharing the Gateway resume through their existing connections. If recovery is exhausted, the task ends with a recoverable error. The chat distinguishes reconnecting from sending a new model request.",
